  "data": {
    "text": "SearchBloom's nine-company ranking includes SearchBloom itself in first place. Five equally-weighted categories produce a 50-point score. The guide checked company websites on October 29, 2026, and case study figures are each company's own reporting. SearchBloom combines SEO, PPC, and CRO with its published merit methodology for AI visibility. Its Custom Closet case reports 51 search leads in September 2026, four months into the engagement, up 122% year-over-year. The partner's CRM recorded 20 of those leads as coming from AI search. SearchBloom positions the SEO works for regulated or service-driven industries. Its DHL case reports AI overview citations rising 287% quarter-on-quarter. SearchBloom positions Tenuity for enterprise brands wanting AI search measurement alongside paid media. Tenuity's Rough Country case reports AI referral traffic up 71% against the previous 90 days. Graphite runs research-based AEO, SEO, and content, with technical SEO recommendations intended for client engineers to implement. Its January 2026 Webflow results report LLM's share of signups doubling from 4% to 8%. SearchBloom positions iPoll rank for complex enterprise sites needing entity and relevance work. Its National Self-Storage case reports AI referred revenue increasing 21% during a three-month pilot. Single Brain combines AEO, SEO, paid media, and content in one team. Its LS Building Products case reports more than 400 additional AI citations after 12 months. SearchBloom positions Siege Media for content and authority gaps rather than technical work. Its Grow Therapy case reports LLM visibility rising from 11% to 43% over the engagement, measured in peak AI. SearchBloom positions Sear Interactive for analytics-driven enterprise AI visibility work. Its Trex case reports owned AI overview references growing from 71 to 199 keywords year-over-year across optimized pages. Amsov adds answer engine optimization and LLM tracking to enterprise SEO. Its OpLoans case reports blog sessions up 263% year-over-year. But Amsov had no published AI search result at the October 29, 2026 check. Only SearchBloom, The SEO Works, and Siege Media publish prices in the ranking. SearchBloom's SEO starts at $3,000 monthly, while The SEO Works publishes four monthly tiers from GBP 1,500 to GBP $6,000 or more. The comparison spans citations, referral traffic, and sign-up share, not one common performance measure. And the results remain company-reported.",
